  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Micro-enterprise training for SILC communities in Gaza and the West Bank</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A consultant will work with CRS and partners to develop a locally relevant micro-enterprise training component, including a training of trainers&apos; format for community mobilisers, private service providers, CRS staff and local partners.  CRS will add this micro-enterprise training to existing and new Savings and Internal Lending Communities (SILC) groups in Gaza with potential expansion of the training model to SILC groups in the West Bank.  

46 people from 4 partners and CRS staff will participate in the training of trainers.  From that training, all SILC groups who have saved successfully for a minimum of 3 months will be given the opportunity to be trained.  The training will also be used in new SILC groups as expansion occurs.</narrative>
  </description>
